;; Seed trust anchors (Task C3, T2c).
;;
;; A map of seed genome id -> expected "sha256:" digest. Each entry
;; pins one seed bundle to its canonical content address (Global
;; Constraint 6: deterministic hashing), so a seed whose bytes changed
;; in ANY way computes a different digest and is refused at load time
;; with :genome/trust-anchor-mismatch.
;;
;; This file is the reference anchors for the shipped seed bundle
;; (genomes/seed). Operators may override the anchors in force via
;; config by passing their own map to
;; evoclj.genome.load/load-genome (see trust-anchors there); when the
;; seed bundle is legitimately regenerated, this file must be updated
;; with the new digest — a stale pin is detected the same way.

{"sha256:de5835d812703df33f707864529c854867807c5120744072207774be316cc096"
 "sha256:de5835d812703df33f707864529c854867807c5120744072207774be316cc096"}
